<title>USA: Norris CEO/President resigns.</title>
<headline>Norris CEO/President resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norris Communications Inc said Friday Chief Executive and President Bob Root has resigned for personal reasons, and Chairman Elwood Norris has taken on the duties of chief executive.</p>
<p>Norris, who has been acting as chairman and chief technical officer, is to relinquish his position as chief technical officer, the company said.</p>
<p>Fred Falk has been named president and will oversee the day-to-day operations of the company.</p>
<p>Formerly, Falk was vice president of business development.</p>
